                        "entry_id": "ffbbfe53-6820-325d-8165-d9253489ea64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various forms of government or rule as designated by words ending in -ocracy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c1bae5a-81f8-46a3-bbf3-d8f868f5c7b4",
                                "sense_id": "a275d503-acd3-361b-9870-2743ad40a93b",
                                "text": "The reason is that you have polities, but other states are mere aggregations of men dwelling together, which are named after their several ruling powers; whereas a state, if an 'ocracy' at all, should be called a theocracy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b0c4aea-8666-47d7-8abb-74189bd6d43a",
                                "sense_id": "a275d503-acd3-361b-9870-2743ad40a93b",
                                "text": "He thundered away about lawsuits and judgments in the High Court of Justice, about disputes with the Court of Chancery, [...] about the insufficiency of the currency, about official aristocracy and all other \"ocracies\" in the world, from King Nebuchadnezzar down to Peter Solvold's democracy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
